From 1edc76e517c77c07f0c026946524dcb6ea71e8d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:31:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ActivityStarter: late-bind mRootWindowContainer instead of
 NPE'ing on boot races
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ActivityStarter captured service.mRootWindowContainer once in its constructor,
into a final field. That reference is still null while
ActivityTaskManagerService is being wired up, so a starter constructed in that
window kept null forever and threw in execute() at
"mRootWindowContainer.getTopDisplayFocusedStack()", taking system_server down
with it:

  NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method
    'com.android.server.wm.ActivityStack com.android.server.wm.RootWindowContainer...'
    at ActivityStarter.execute(ActivityStarter.java:654)
    at ActivityStartController.startHomeActivity(ActivityStartController.java:206)

Registering the mini-HDMI external display before the framework had settled hit
this reproducibly — it is the crash hdmi_up.sh has always warned about ("NOT
during boot — registering an external display inside systemReady NPE-crash-loops
system_server"), and it also killed the framework when the new Mapper-button
recovery re-dispatched a bring-up while system_server was still bouncing.

Verified: with HDMI brought up during boot, system_server keeps its pid, boots to
a usable launcher, and the new guard reports 6 aborted start requests instead of
crashing; a normal post-boot bring-up registers display 1 with zero guard hits
and zero NPEs, so steady-state behaviour is unchanged.

Changes:
- Make `mRootWindowContainer` non-final and bind it lazily at the top of `execute()`, aborting the request with `START_ABORTED` (and a warning) if the container genuinely does not exist yet, so the caller can retry once the display settles

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I9bdcb668af1fcb1ccbda6c97541eac03dd48afae
---
 .../android/server/wm/ActivityStarter.java    | 25 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityStarter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityStarter.java
index 20b6b468..d78388ef 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityStarter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityStarter.java
@@ -142,7 +142,14 @@ class ActivityStarter {
     private static final int INVALID_LAUNCH_MODE = -1;
 
     private final ActivityTaskManagerService mService;
-    private final RootWindowContainer mRootWindowContainer;
+    // GPD XD+: NOT final. This used to be captured once in the constructor
+    // from service.mRootWindowContainer, which is still null while
+    // ActivityTaskManagerService is being wired up. A starter constructed in that
+    // window kept a null reference forever and NPE'd in execute(), taking
+    // system_server down — reproducibly hit by registering the mini-HDMI external
+    // display before the framework had settled, which is why hdmi_up.sh warns
+    // never to bring the mirror up during boot. Bound lazily in execute() instead.
+    private RootWindowContainer mRootWindowContainer;
     private final ActivityStackSupervisor mSupervisor;
     private final ActivityStartInterceptor mInterceptor;
     private final ActivityStartController mController;
@@ -632,6 +639,22 @@ class ActivityStarter {
                 throw new IllegalArgumentException("File descriptors passed in Intent");
             }
 
+            // GPD XD+: late-bind the root window container. It is null if this
+            // starter was constructed before ActivityTaskManagerService finished
+            // wiring up; by the time a request is actually executed it is normally
+            // set, so pick it up here rather than NPE'ing below on a stale null.
+            if (mRootWindowContainer == null) {
+                mRootWindowContainer = mService.mRootWindowContainer;
+                if (mRootWindowContainer == null) {
+                    // Genuinely too early to start anything. Abort this request
+                    // instead of crashing system_server; the caller (e.g.
+                    // startHomeActivity) retries once the display settles.
+                    Slog.w(TAG, "execute: no RootWindowContainer yet, aborting "
+                            + mRequest.intent);
+                    return START_ABORTED;
+                }
+            }
+
             final LaunchingState launchingState;
             synchronized (mService.mGlobalLock) {
                 final ActivityRecord caller = ActivityRecord.forTokenLocked(mRequest.resultTo);
-- 
